
Task: “Simple Jewel Bill” App
Goal:

Show a list of jewelry items in a RecyclerView.

When the user taps an item, open another screen (Activity) that shows a simple bill for that single item.

That’s it:
1 list screen → 1 bill screen using Intent.

Screens
1. MainActivity – Item Lists
One RecyclerView.

Each row shows:

Jewelry name (e.g., “Gold Ring”)

Price (e.g., “₹25,000”)

On item click:

Open BillActivity using an Intent.

Pass:

name

price

Example data:

kotlin
data class JewelItem(
    val name: String,
    val price: String
)

val jewelList = listOf(
    JewelItem("Gold Ring", "25000"),
    JewelItem("Pearl Necklace", "45000"),
    JewelItem("Diamond Earrings", "80000")
)
2. BillActivity – Simple Bill
Receives name and price from Intent.

Shows:

Title: “Bill”

Item name

Price

A fixed tax (for simplicity, e.g., 10%)

Total = price + tax

Example calculation (in code):

kotlin
val priceValue = priceString.toLong()
val tax = priceValue * 10 / 100
val total = priceValue + tax
Display:

Item: Gold Ring

Price: ₹25,000

Tax (10%): ₹2,500

Total: ₹27,500

No cart, no quantity, just one item → one bill.

How Intent Is Used
From MainActivity:

kotlin
val intent = Intent(this, BillActivity::class.java).apply {
    putExtra("EXTRA_NAME", item.name)
    putExtra("EXTRA_PRICE", item.price)
}
startActivity(intent)
In BillActivity:

kotlin
val name = intent.getStringExtra("EXTRA_NAME") ?: ""
val priceString = intent.getStringExtra("EXTRA_PRICE") ?: "0"
Then compute tax and total and show in TextViews.

What You Practice
Creating a simple RecyclerView with a list.

Handling item click in RecyclerView.

Starting a new Activity with an Intent.

Passing simple data (String) via Intent.putExtra.

Doing a basic calculation (tax & total) and displaying it.

